*Gerry Beltgens, May 6, 2023*

On May 4th 2023, after months of preparation, we loaded the first of two 40 ft. containers with computers and hospital equipment for Guatemala.

This load included 28 pallets of computers and monitors (around 800 computers), 12 hospital beds, 32 mattresses, and hundreds of boxes of assorted medical equipment including wheelchairs, hygiene kits, gowns, sponges, gloves, facemasks, walkers, and even a couple of kids’ bicycles.

The people and organisations involved included Gerry Beltgens with Access to Education Collaborative, Dr. Joe Delvicario from Health for Humanity, Jerry Zdril and Dan Gallant from Rotary World Help and many other volunteers. Funding was provided by donations from the Rotary Club of Chatham, Ontario, the Rotary Club of Gig Harbor and Health for Humanity.

The computers were donated by Royal Roads University and Douglas College as they replaced their older computers. These computers will be refurbished by students in Guatemala at a Computer Tech Training Program that we set up last year with funding support from the Rotary Club of Victoria Harbourside. Once refurbished and upgraded these computers will be made available to Rotary and other non-profit projects in Guatemala.

The medical equipment is going to Obras Sociales Hermano Pedro Hospital in Antigua Guatemala.

